/*****************************************************************************
    Rulings of record (all Tony)
*****************************************************************************/
Inheritance and style:= -- in Topics/forms ("Inheritance, one rule"; "style:= is the only spelling"): text properties inherit, box properties do not; the floor refuses a style that is not held.
Italic (2026-11-11, SEQ 624 W1)
    A text property: a bare italic on a field or in its style draws the font's italic face, and it inherits. italic=off turns it off below: RULED AS INTERIM (Tony, 2026-11-11, SEQ 625 R0) -- it stands until typesetting's {style: text} runs exist, when it is revisited. (A 0 cannot be told from absent in kant's climb.)
    A font with no italic face warns by name and draws upright. The old GUI: italic was a font-style mask (traits: italic=1) that converted the field's font (GUI/Stylish.twk, fONTstyle); Bot's PDF road looked for a font file named Italic.
Shadow (2026-11-11, SEQ 622 R3)
    A field attribute, applied wherever a form names it. The old Stylish values: 2 right, 2 down, blur 3, black at 30%. One shadow per field (ruled, SEQ 623 R1): its fill if it has one, else its border, else its text.
    A fill's shadow falls outside the frame, so a neighbour drawn later can cover it. No attribute changes the values yet; no form asks.
Opacity (2026-11-11, SEQ 623)
    opacity=n, a number from 0 (clear) to 1 (opaque), a box property: the field's own fill, border and text are drawn at it. A value outside 0 to 1 refuses by name and draws opaque. An image is not covered yet.
    opacity=0 draws fully clear, on a fill, a border, text, and from a style (measured, SEQ 625 C1; opacityT OP-6): the floor asks whether the attribute exists, not whether its value is true. Nothing to cure.
    No form spells opacity. The layers form is Windows/cards ("Cards and Layers"); its third card says "Layers not enabled for now" and names layers, nothing else.
    The old GUI's spelling was transparency=n on a field or a colour entry, handed straight to the fill colour as its alpha (GUI/Stuff/Filler.twk); no form uses that either.
    layers and overlay are layout orientations: the members share the parent's full box (old GUI Details.twk). That is why the census lists them under pure kant -- placement and draw order, no floor change.
Text, colours and fonts (2026-11-05 to 2026-11-10)
    A field takes font and color from its own attribute, else its style, else its enclosing fields. color falls back to black, the font to Helvetica 12.
    A field's text is its own string value; if it holds a group, the group's text, one level only. A describe attribute, when present, is the text drawn.
    Text that does not fit is clipped between words, with a warning naming the field.
    IncantForms/Controls/styles holds the 14 colours and 7 fonts; tests load it explicitly. setColor skips a leading #.
    A fill reader takes the held field, never its name. No colour cache.
Images (2026-11-10)
    image="path". The only fit is fill: cover the frame keeping the shape, centred, cropped. An image field's text is its description and is never drawn.
Box attributes
    rounded (2026-11-11, SEQ 621 R2): a number in points, the corner radius, on a field or its style like any other style attribute. A bare rounded takes the default, which lives in the default style
        (defaultStyle in IncantForms/Controls/styles, registry sTYLEs): 5, the old GUI's default (GUI/Control.twk; Bot's PDF road used 8). Built so: the field's own rounded, else its style's; not inherited
        from the enclosing field (as fill is not); a radius past half the short side draws at half; a value that is not a number refuses by name and draws square.
    Border sides: topBorder, bottomBorder, leftBorder, rightBorder; bare is width 1, =number sets it; naming any side draws only the named sides.
    fill is not inherited. A bare number is in points (1/72 inch).

